Heartworms has shared a new single, ‘The Window’ – you can listen to it below.

The song follows on from the London goth rock artist’s previous track, ‘Guess I’m Stuck In The Dark’, which was released last month. It followed on from her acclaimed 2025 debut album, ‘Glutton For Punishment’ .

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

“‘The Window’ is my effort to understand the spiritual idea of the interior castle, to reach God even when there was only silence,” explained the former NME Cover star (real name Jojo Orme).

‘A window can illuminate, obscure, reveal and reflect – the song acts as a metaphor for time, escape, limitlessness, self-reflection and rebirth.”

Produced by collaborator Dan Carey, ‘The Window’ hears Heartworms howl in the chorus: “ I don’t know if I’ll get out OK (can’t do enough to beat you)/ I don’t know if I’ll get out OK (can’t do enough to beat you)/ Oh, I don’t know if I don’t know my name (can’t do enough to beat you)/ God, I hope that I find out… ”

